<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T4.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="S4.T4.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">Ablation on the pseudo-labeler.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Two-headed Classifier:</span> To evaluate the impact of text prompt initialization for our two classifiers, <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\text{LLM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mtext>LLM</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\text{LLM}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\text{LLM}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mtext>LLM</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\text{LLM}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, we conduct an ablation study on various strategies, as detailed in <a href="#S4.T5" title="In 4.2 Ablation Studies ‣ 4 Experiments and Analyses ‣ microCLIP: Unsupervised CLIP Adaptation via Coarse-Fine Token Fusion for Fine-Grained Image Classification" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. We employ the same prompt ensembling technique as CLIP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite> for class-specific handcrafted prompts. Consistent with WCA’s design choices <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>, we exclude the ablation where handcrafted prompts are used for a fixed <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\text{LLM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mtext>LLM</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\text{LLM}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The results demonstrate that our method achieves superior performance across the ablation datasets, with overall accuracy gains of <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.03\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.03</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.03\%</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.99\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.99</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.99\%</annotation></semantics></math> compared to the two ablation settings.</p>
</div>
